                                                                                                                      "value":  "Dowry deaths are the control."
                                                                                                                  },
                                                                                                                  {
                                                                                                                      "textStyle":  {
                                                                                                                                        "fontSize":  "10pt"
                                                                                                                                    },
                                                                                                                      "value":  "\n\nEvery head grew except dowry deaths: 6,738 in 2001, 6,753 in 2021. Deaths are the hardest category to under-report, so flat deaths against a 178% rise in cruelty complaints argues that much of the growth is rising reporting propensity rather than rising incidence.\n\nThat is an argument, not a proof. This data cannot separate the two."
